# Register K32. The query was `((inherited) @warn)` -- it matched EVERY inherited
# node, so a qualified call raised a finding whose own message says BARE.
# Line 45 is the only bare `inherited;` in the fixture.
inherited-bare 45
# The two QUALIFIED forms must not fire. Both are (rule, line) pairs rather than
# a blanket !inherited-bare, because the rule DOES fire in this file: a blanket
# form would be satisfied only by the rule never firing at all, and asserting
# that would contradict the line above.
#
# v(ADP3 T4f fix round 1): the first pin named line 39, which is `begin`. NOTHING
# has ever fired there -- the pre-K32 query `((inherited) @warn)` fires at 40, 45
# and 50, the current one at 45 -- so the pin was satisfied before and after the
# fix and could not fail. The qualified paren-less call is on line 40.
# Executed both ways with `lint --rules-dir` over a scratch copy of rules\:
#   old `((inherited) @warn)`  -> inherited-bare at 40, 45, 50
#   current query              -> inherited-bare at 45
!inherited-bare 40
!inherited-bare 50
